# Images inside a text (reference/common/text-formatting.md#images-inside-a-text). Pages of 595 × 300 with margins
# of 40: page area of 515 × 220 from (40, 40). Lines of 12 (Size 10), baseline 9 below the top of the line and
# capitals of 0.7 × 10 = 7, so an image is centered 3.5 above the baseline: 5.5 below the top of the line.
#
# An image is as tall as the Size (10) and as wide as its proportion gives (square.png is square, shapes.svg is
# 200 × 100), measured as a word: p1 is one line, "Marca " (30) + 20 + " y fin" (30). p2 is 60 wide: "aaa " (20) +
# 10 + " bbb" (20) = 50 fit, "ccc" does not: two lines. In p3 the image is glued to its letters: one word of
# 20 + 10 + 10. In p4 the image is inside a link (clickable, with its Alt) and followed by " web".
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 595
		Height: 300
		Margin: 40
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Markup: markdown
	Section:
		Text: Marca ![Logo](test/shapes.svg) y fin
			Id: p1
		Text: aaa ![Un cuadrado](test/square.png) bbb ccc
			Id: p2
			Box:
				Width: 60
		Text: Pega![](test/square.png)do
			Id: p3
		Text: [![Web](test/check.svg)](https://stxt.dev) web
			Id: p4
